+// E011 (patch 0002): the control socket's binary channel F1 (SPEEDRUN_WIRE=bin) and the state block F2
+// (experiments/E011-speed/plan.md "Binary formats"; experiments/E011-speed/engine/WIRE.md is the reference).
+//
+// The commands are those of the JSON protocol (speedrun_control.cpp), one message each way, with the same checks and
+// the same effects; only the encoding differs. Framing: u32 payload length, u8 type, the payload. A payload holds
+// fmi-core's types in declaration order: integers at their width, little-endian; bool u8 0/1; Option u8 0 or 1 then
+// the value; Vec and String a u32 count then the items (UTF-8 bytes); an enum a u8 variant index then its fields.
+//
+// Two additions over the JSON protocol: State (the F2 block: what facts_of reads, as flat arrays) and Step (run N
+// frames, then reply with the stop status, the F2 block or its delta from the last one sent on this connection, and
+// the runs and explain entries recorded meanwhile, in one message).
+//
+// Observation only, as the JSON dumps: the encoders read engine members and call the const members the JSON dumps
+// call. Without names, the binary dumps call fewer of them (no getObjOrActorName, no verb text).
+
+#define FORBIDDEN_SYMBOL_ALLOW_ALL
